# SPA deep links. Any route that is not a real file (/, /admin, /security and their
# sub-paths) returns the built index.html with a 200 so the client router decides.
#
# Do NOT add exact rules such as `/security /index.html 200`: rewriting a clean path
# to /index.html makes Pages canonicalise it to `/`, so the live site answered
# /security and /admin with a 308 to the homepage and the dashboards were unreachable.
# /api/* and /media/* still run as Pages Functions first (see _routes.json).
/*          /index.html   200
